# ---------- I. own calculations ----------
F("OWN CALCULATION (confirms the project record): the Timoshenko factor f(m,n)=6(1+m)^2/[3(1+m)^2+(1+mn)(m^2+1/(mn))] evaluates to exactly 1.5 at m=n^-1/2 for n = 1, 3.2, 160 and 1724 (checked numerically in calc.py to 12 decimals). The Lean proof itself was not re-run.",
  "calc", "high", json.dumps(CALC["ceiling_check_f_at_m=n^-1/2"]))
pairs = {r["passive"]: r for r in CALC["pairs_h1mm"]}
F("OWN CALCULATION, NEW: for a 1.0 mm strip with Flexible 80A V2 as the active layer, the thickness of the passive layer needed to reach the ceiling (m = n^-1/2, m = passive/active thickness, n = passive/active modulus) is 0.073 mm for Tough 1000, 0.024 mm for Rigid 10K, 0.64 mm for Flexible 50A and 0.73 mm for Silicone 40A. Moduli are Tough 1000 932 MPa and Rigid 10K 10,000 MPa (Formlabs pages) and secant estimates 5.8 / 1.8 / 0.8 MPa for Flexible 80A V2 / 50A / Silicone 40A (stress at 50 % strain divided by 0.5, from the project record; NOT small-strain moduli, and the swollen layer is softer). The two stiff passives therefore need layers far below the 0.2 mm printable-wall figure; Rigid 10K is a poor passive partner at any printable thickness (f = 0.29 at 0.2 mm).",
  "calc", "medium", json.dumps({k: {kk: v for kk, v in r.items() if kk.startswith(("h_passive", "f("))} for k, r in pairs.items()}), src2=["project"])
F("OWN CALCULATION, NEW: with Tough 1000 passive / Flexible 80A V2 active at 1.0 mm total, f falls steeply with the passive layer thickness: 1.49 at 0.05-0.10 mm, 1.36 at 0.15, 1.13 at 0.20, 0.86 at 0.25, 0.61 at 0.30 mm. A 0.1 mm Z error in a 0.2 mm layer (see on-platform compression) moves f by about 0.3 to 0.4, i.e. the thin passive layer's printed thickness must be measured on every strip.",
  "calc", "medium", json.dumps(CALC["sensitivity_f_Tough1000_passive_h1mm"]))
F("OWN CALCULATION: if the Flexible 80A V2 slab volume gains (+3 % at 1 day, +7 % at 1 week in water) were isotropic and the passive layer did not swell, the free linear strain would be 0.99 % and 2.28 %; at the ceiling (f=1.5, h=1.0 mm) curvature is 14.9 and 34.2 1/m (radius 67 and 29 mm; 40 mm strip tip rises 11.5 and 23.4 mm). At f = 0.5 the 1-day tip rise is 4.0 mm. Isotropy, equilibrium of the slab and the volume column's reliability (see additivity check) are all assumptions.",
  "calc", "low", json.dumps({k: CALC[k] for k in ("curvature_h1mm_water_1 day", "curvature_h1mm_water_1 week")}))
F("OWN CALCULATION: residual curl from printing is not small against the signal. A strip whose tip sags 1 mm over 40 mm has curvature 1.25 1/m, equal to the ceiling signal of a 0.083 % differential strain at h = 1 mm; 0.5 mm sag = 0.62 1/m. Any control that cannot resolve ~0.3 1/m (0.25 mm tip sag) cannot see a 0.1 % strain.",
  "calc", "medium", json.dumps({"tip_sag_to_kappa_1/m": CALC["residual_curl_from_tip_sag"], "eq_deps_for_1mm_sag_%": CALC["eq_deps_for_1mm_sag_%"]}))
F("OWN CALCULATION (scaling estimate, assumes Fickian uptake with constant diffusivity): a 1 cm cube is slow to fill because time scales with half-thickness squared. A 1.0 mm strip reaches in 14 min the uptake a cube reaches in 24 h; a 0.4 mm strip in 2.3 min. So a 20 min Flexible 50A IPA wash is equivalent to about 33 h (1.0 mm) or 208 h (0.4 mm) of cube soak, i.e. above the 39.2 % 24 h cube figure; the 10 min Flexible 80A V2 wash is equivalent to 17 h or 104 h. Formlabs' own wash limits (Elastic 50A V1: 'avoid washing longer than 20 minutes, as this may degrade parts') are consistent with this. No diffusivity was measured.",
  "calc", "low", json.dumps({k: CALC[k] for k in ("thin_strip_equivalent_time_to_cube_24h_min", "wash_equivalent_cube_hours")}))
F("OWN CALCULATION: data-sheet mass versus volume for Flexible 80A V2 is inconsistent with simple volume additivity (resin density 1.04 g/mL from the data sheet; IPA density 0.785 is unverified background). Water 1 day: +8 % mass predicts +8.3 % volume, reported +3 %. IPA 1 day: +45 % mass predicts +60 % volume, reported +113 %. The strain inputs to any bilayer prediction should be measured on the strips, not taken from this table.",
  "calc", "medium", json.dumps(CALC["tds_mass_vs_volume_additivity"]))
F("OWN CALCULATION: layer count. At 100 um layers (the minimum listed for Flexible 50A, Silicone 40A) a 0.2 mm layer is 2 layers and a 1.0 mm strip 10 layers; thickness is quantised to the layer height, and the 0.1 mm on-platform compression equals one such layer.",
  "calc", "medium", json.dumps(CALC["layers_per_thickness"]["layer=0.1 mm"]))

